00:17:09,404 --> 00:17:10,739
You want to go?

284
00:17:10,822 --> 00:17:11,865
No, thanks.

285
00:17:11,990 --> 00:17:13,616
I want a full
report, though.

286
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:14,784
Later.

287
00:17:14,826 --> 00:17:15,910
Yeah.

288
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:22,876
Well, I loved it.

289
00:17:23,001 --> 00:17:25,462
I was spellbound
the whole time.

290
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:26,880
I could tell.

291
00:17:27,005 --> 00:17:28,465
So could
everyone else

292
00:17:28,548 --> 00:17:31,051
with that resonating
snore of yours.

293
00:17:36,181 --> 00:17:38,641
Did I tell you
what Melissa said?

294
00:17:38,725 --> 00:17:40,060
Yeah, about six times.

295
00:17:40,185 --> 00:17:41,644
It wasn't six times.

296
00:17:41,728 --> 00:17:44,064
Quit being
so blase about this.

297
00:17:44,189 --> 00:17:45,648
This is really
important.

298
00:17:45,732 --> 00:17:48,068
I'll have two pieces
in her gallery.

299
00:17:48,193 --> 00:17:52,113
The New York Times
reviews her gallery all the time.

300
00:17:52,197 --> 00:17:53,698
Molly,
The New York Times

301
00:17:53,782 --> 00:17:55,700
is just some
frustrated little critic

302
00:17:55,784 --> 00:17:59,037
with pimples on his ass
who flunked art school.

303
00:17:59,162 --> 00:18:00,497
Who cares what they think?

304
00:18:00,622 --> 00:18:02,957
About eight million
readers, that's who.

305
00:18:03,041 --> 00:18:06,836
Nah, they're just
reading the sports page.

306
00:18:06,961 --> 00:18:08,880
Your work
is really beautiful.

307
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:10,465
It really is.

308
00:18:10,548 --> 00:18:11,591
Thanks.

309
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:14,010
It shouldn't matter
what anyone else thinks,

310
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:15,595
just what I think.

311
00:18:20,684 --> 00:18:23,019
I want
to marry you, Sam.

312
00:18:23,103 --> 00:18:24,437
What?

313
00:18:24,562 --> 00:18:26,815
What?

314
00:18:26,898 --> 00:18:28,483
Yep.

315
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:30,860
I've been
thinking about it.

316
00:18:30,902 --> 00:18:33,405
I've been thinking
about it a lot,

317
00:18:33,530 --> 00:18:36,658
and I think we
should just do it.

318
00:18:36,741 --> 00:18:38,535
You're serious.

319
00:18:38,576 --> 00:18:39,994
Yeah.

320
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:45,542
What's that look for?

321
00:18:50,130 --> 00:18:53,591
You never wanted
to talk about it.

322
00:19:02,767 --> 00:19:05,061
Do you love me, Sam?

323
00:19:05,145 --> 00:19:08,189
Well, what do you think?

324
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,233
Why don't you
ever say it?

325
00:19:10,442 --> 00:19:13,778
What do you mean?
I say it all the time.

326
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:15,238
No, you say ''ditto,''

327
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:17,574
and that's
not the same.

328
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:22,120
People say I love you
all the time,

329
00:19:22,203 --> 00:19:24,622
and it doesn't
mean anything.

330
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:30,128
You know, sometimes
you need to hear it.

331
00:19:31,504 --> 00:19:33,256
I need to hear it.

332
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:36,092
Let's go.

333
00:19:44,768 --> 00:19:46,102
What should we do?

334
00:19:46,144 --> 00:19:47,645
Let me handle it.

335
00:19:47,812 --> 00:19:49,105
What do you want?

336
00:19:49,230 --> 00:19:51,149
Your wallet--
give it to me!

337
00:19:51,232 --> 00:19:54,277
Sam, just give it to him.

338
00:19:55,904 --> 00:19:58,990
OK, just take the money.
Just leave--

339
00:19:59,074 --> 00:20:00,825
No, Sam--

340
00:20:00,909 --> 00:20:02,827
You son of a bitch!

341
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,831
Sam, don't!

342
00:20:08,166 --> 00:20:09,626
Somebody help us!

343
00:20:09,751 --> 00:20:11,795
Jesus Christ, Sam!

344
00:20:13,004 --> 00:20:14,631
Just get off him.

345
00:20:14,756 --> 00:20:16,341
Somebody!

346
00:20:16,633 --> 00:20:18,301
Somebody help us!

347
00:20:18,593 --> 00:20:20,178
Sam, just let...

348
00:20:21,388 --> 00:20:23,181
Sam, stop it.

349
00:20:23,348 --> 00:20:24,808
Stop it, Sam!

350
00:20:24,933 --> 00:20:26,643
[Gunshot]

351
00:20:45,078 --> 00:20:46,246
Molly?

352
00:20:48,915 --> 00:20:50,250
Molly, he got--

353
00:20:57,048 --> 00:20:58,216
Sam...

354
00:21:02,721 --> 00:21:04,889
Baby, hold on.

355
00:21:05,015 --> 00:21:06,933
You're going
to be OK.

356
00:21:09,102 --> 00:21:10,353
Somebody?

357
00:21:10,645 --> 00:21:12,188
Somebody?

358
00:21:12,313 --> 00:21:14,190
Somebody help us!

359
00:21:14,274 --> 00:21:15,692
Oh, Sam.

360
00:21:17,694 --> 00:21:19,029
Oh, my God.

361
00:21:19,112 --> 00:21:21,031
Oh, Sam, come on.

362
00:21:21,114 --> 00:21:22,699
Hold on, baby.

363
00:21:22,782 --> 00:21:25,076
Someone's going to come.

364
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:27,787
You're going to be OK.

365
00:21:37,714 --> 00:21:39,299
Somebody!

366
00:21:39,382 --> 00:21:42,052
Somebody help me!

367
00:21:42,177 --> 00:21:44,179
Please, anybody!

368
00:21:44,304 --> 00:21:46,264
Help me. Please help me.

369
00:21:46,389 --> 00:21:48,350
Take it easy, all right?

370
00:21:49,976 --> 00:21:51,311
We'll help you, OK?

371
00:21:51,394 --> 00:21:54,022
Molly? Molly?

372
00:21:54,105 --> 00:21:55,231
Molly?

373
00:21:58,360 --> 00:21:59,361
OK.

374
00:21:59,652 --> 00:22:00,904
All right.
All right.

375
00:22:00,987 --> 00:22:02,197
Molly?

376
00:22:02,322 --> 00:22:03,782
What should we do?

377
00:22:03,907 --> 00:22:04,908
Aah!

378
00:22:07,285 --> 00:22:08,161
Aah!

379
00:22:08,286 --> 00:22:11,456
Aah!

380
00:22:13,124 --> 00:22:15,001
What's happening?

381
00:22:16,127 --> 00:22:17,712
What's...

382
00:22:17,837 --> 00:22:19,005
Is he breathing?

383
00:22:22,801 --> 00:22:24,969
I don't know
if he's breathing.

384
00:22:26,054 --> 00:22:28,473
Don't die, Sam.
Hold on.

385
00:22:28,723 --> 00:22:30,767
Hold on, baby.
Hold on.

386
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:32,185
Oh, my God.

387
00:22:48,993 --> 00:22:50,829
Come on, man.

388
00:22:50,954 --> 00:22:52,247
All right.

389
00:22:52,330 --> 00:22:54,541
Here we go.

390
00:22:54,791 --> 00:22:56,376
1 ...

391
00:22:56,459 --> 00:22:58,336
Come on, baby.

392
00:22:58,461 --> 00:23:00,922
Sam, don't you leave me.

393
00:23:01,006 --> 00:23:02,465
Sam, hold on!

394
00:23:03,717 --> 00:23:04,926
Sam...

395
00:23:05,010 --> 00:23:06,177
Oh, Sam...

396
00:23:08,430 --> 00:23:09,764
Jesus...

397
00:23:56,478 --> 00:23:59,356
Miss Jensen, if you'll just step
this way, please.

398
00:24:16,498 --> 00:24:19,084
So, what happened
to you?

399
00:24:20,251 --> 00:24:21,211
What?

400
00:24:21,378 --> 00:24:23,254
You're new, huh?
I could tell.

401
00:24:23,380 --> 00:24:25,382
Are you talking to me?

402
00:24:25,507 --> 00:24:26,966
Relax. It ain't
like before.

403
00:24:27,092 --> 00:24:30,011
It's a whole new
ball of wax.

404
00:24:30,136 --> 00:24:32,013
Who are you?

405
00:24:32,097 --> 00:24:34,015
I'm waiting
for my wife.

406
00:24:34,099 --> 00:24:37,018
She's in the cardiac wing.
She's fighting it.

407
00:24:46,111 --> 00:24:47,404
Shot, huh?

408
00:24:47,487 --> 00:24:48,863
That'll do it every time.

409
00:24:50,448 --> 00:24:51,449
Poor bastard.

410
00:24:51,616 --> 00:24:54,202
You may as well
get used to it.

411
00:24:54,327 --> 00:24:56,663
You could be here
for a long while.

412
00:25:00,959 --> 00:25:03,294
Come here.
I'll tell you a secret.

413
00:25:03,420 --> 00:25:04,879
Doors ain't so bad.

414
00:25:05,005 --> 00:25:06,923
Zip, zap--
they ain't nothing.

415
00:25:07,007 --> 00:25:08,925
You'll see.
You'll catch on.

416
00:25:09,009 --> 00:25:11,344
This patient's fibrillating.
Let's move it.

417
00:25:11,428 --> 00:25:13,847
Give me
the paddles.

418
00:25:13,972 --> 00:25:15,849
He ain't
going to make it.

419
00:25:15,974 --> 00:25:17,934
I've seen it
a million times.

420
00:25:18,018 --> 00:25:19,352
He's a goner.

421
00:25:19,436 --> 00:25:20,895
He's still
fibrillating.

422
00:25:21,021 --> 00:25:22,063
Clear.

423
00:25:24,649 --> 00:25:26,026
You see?

424
00:25:26,109 --> 00:25:27,444
Here they come.

425
00:25:31,364 --> 00:25:33,033
Lucky bastard.

426
00:25:33,158 --> 00:25:36,077
It could have been
the other ones.

427
00:25:36,161 --> 00:25:38,413
You never know.

428
00:25:58,683 --> 00:25:59,601
Who are--

429
00:26:05,190 --> 00:26:06,941
No!

430
00:26:13,031 --> 00:26:14,115
Aah!

431
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:15,575
God help me.

432
00:26:17,243 --> 00:26:19,079
Oh, God...

433
00:26:19,162 --> 00:26:20,497
help me.

434
00:26:26,670 --> 00:26:29,631
''I am sunk
in the abysmal swamp

435
00:26:29,714 --> 00:26:31,633
where there is no foothold.

436
00:26:31,716 --> 00:26:34,511
I have reached
the watery depths.

437
00:26:34,594 --> 00:26:37,555
The flood overwhelms me.

438
00:26:37,681 --> 00:26:41,142
I am wearied with calling.''

439
00:26:41,226 --> 00:26:44,646
As we say farewell
to our friend Sam Wheat,

440
00:26:44,979 --> 00:26:47,315
we are reminded
of his kindness...

441
00:26:48,775 --> 00:26:51,319
his generosity,

442
00:26:51,403 --> 00:26:54,447
his buoyancy of spirit.

443
00:26:54,531 --> 00:26:56,157
All that we treasure--

444
00:26:56,241 --> 00:26:58,576
our loved ones,

445
00:26:58,702 --> 00:26:59,953
our friends,

446
00:27:00,078 --> 00:27:02,038
our body,

447
00:27:02,205 --> 00:27:04,874
our mind--

448
00:27:05,041 --> 00:27:07,377
are but on loan to us.

449
00:27:07,460 --> 00:27:10,422
We must
surrender them all.

450
00:27:10,547 --> 00:27:13,466
We are all travelers
on the same road,

451
00:27:13,550 --> 00:27:16,094
which leads
to the same end.

452
00:27:19,681 --> 00:27:23,184
As our loved one
enters eternal life,

453
00:27:23,309 --> 00:27:25,937
let us remember
that love, too, is eternal.

454
00:27:27,689 --> 00:27:30,150
That although
we will miss him,

455
00:27:30,275 --> 00:27:32,277
our love
will light the void

456
00:27:32,360 --> 00:27:34,279
and dispel the darkness.

457
00:28:13,651 --> 00:28:16,196
I picked up
your shirts today.

458
00:28:16,321 --> 00:28:19,449
I don't know why.

459
00:28:23,661 --> 00:28:27,290
Mr. Reynolds told me
to tell you hello.

460
00:28:30,335 --> 00:28:32,295
I broke into tears.

461
00:28:35,548 --> 00:28:38,468
It's like I think
about you every minute.

462
00:28:38,551 --> 00:28:41,721
It's like
I can still feel you.

463
00:28:51,439 --> 00:28:53,650
I'm here, Moll.

464
00:28:53,858 --> 00:28:55,110
[Hisses]

465
00:29:00,740 --> 00:29:02,117
[Meowwr]

466
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:04,119
Floyd, what's
the matter, kitty?

467
00:29:04,202 --> 00:29:05,578
What's the matter?

468
00:29:05,704 --> 00:29:08,665
Crazy cat.

469
00:29:12,794 --> 00:29:14,504
Sam?

470
00:29:17,340 --> 00:29:19,259
That's really
stupid.

471
00:29:30,562 --> 00:29:32,063
I love this picture.

472
00:29:32,188 --> 00:29:33,106
It's great.

473
00:29:33,189 --> 00:29:36,234
Office.

474
00:29:44,909 --> 00:29:45,160
Let me see that.

475
00:29:46,745 --> 00:29:47,662
It's, um...

476
00:29:47,746 --> 00:29:49,205
Sam's address book.

477
00:29:49,372 --> 00:29:50,290
Right.

478
00:29:56,421 --> 00:29:57,714
Dave Brubeck.
Newport, '88.

479
00:29:57,839 --> 00:29:59,341
Should I toss
them?

480
00:29:59,424 --> 00:30:00,342
No.

481
00:30:00,425 --> 00:30:04,346
No? Molly, we hated
that concert.

482
00:30:04,512 --> 00:30:05,388
Hey.

483
00:30:05,513 --> 00:30:08,558
Oh. You wanted
to save those?

484
00:30:08,683 --> 00:30:10,185
Rolaids?

485
00:30:10,310 --> 00:30:12,854
Molly, what
are you doing?

486
00:30:20,612 --> 00:30:24,366
I just miss him,
Carl.

487
00:30:24,449 --> 00:30:25,825
Me, too.

488
00:30:28,620 --> 00:30:29,746
Carl?

489
00:30:29,871 --> 00:30:30,747
Yeah?

490
00:30:30,872 --> 00:30:32,374
Wait a minute.
Wait.

491
00:30:32,457 --> 00:30:33,375
What?

492
00:30:33,458 --> 00:30:34,751
Not that one.

493
00:30:34,876 --> 00:30:36,378
Which? Oh, I'm sorry.

494
00:30:36,461 --> 00:30:38,755
I didn't mean to put
that on there.

495
00:30:38,922 --> 00:30:40,382
That's OK.

496
00:30:40,465 --> 00:30:42,842
Hey, Moll,
why don't you come?

497
00:30:42,967 --> 00:30:44,427
It's like summer
outside.

498
00:30:44,511 --> 00:30:47,764
No, I'm really
not up for it.

499
00:30:47,889 --> 00:30:49,766
Just for a walk.

500
00:30:49,849 --> 00:30:51,351
I don't want to.

501
00:30:51,476 --> 00:30:53,520
You can't stay in
all day.

502
00:30:53,645 --> 00:30:54,771
It's not healthy.

503
00:30:54,896 --> 00:30:56,898
Carl, I can't do it!

504
00:30:57,023 --> 00:30:59,818
Molly, you're not
the one who died.

505
00:31:01,986 --> 00:31:03,905
I'm sorry.

506
00:31:03,988 --> 00:31:05,448
Don't apologize.

507
00:31:05,573 --> 00:31:07,784
Shit.

508
00:31:11,496 --> 00:31:13,248
Maybe you're right.

509
00:31:13,373 --> 00:31:14,874
Maybe
just a short one.

510
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:16,960
That a girl.

511
00:31:19,295 --> 00:31:20,463
I'm sorry.

512
00:31:20,547 --> 00:31:22,716
Don't worry about it.

513
00:31:22,841 --> 00:31:24,217
Molly!

514
00:32:23,902 --> 00:32:26,404
What are you
doing here?

515
00:32:26,571 --> 00:32:28,865
You bastard.

516
00:32:31,117 --> 00:32:34,079
You son of a bitch!

517
00:32:49,844 --> 00:32:52,055
What do you want?

518
00:32:53,390 --> 00:32:54,849
-[Door Opening]
-Molly?

519
00:32:56,059 --> 00:32:58,853
Molly, get out!

520
00:32:58,937 --> 00:32:59,979
Oh, my God.

521
00:33:04,776 --> 00:33:08,029
No, Molly! Look,
no, no, please!

522
00:33:10,448 --> 00:33:11,366
Molly!

523
00:33:11,449 --> 00:33:12,617
Molly,
he's got a gun!

524
00:33:12,784 --> 00:33:13,660
[Meow]

525
00:33:13,785 --> 00:33:15,995
Hi, kitty. Hi.

526
00:33:16,121 --> 00:33:18,415
You hurt her--

527
00:33:43,189 --> 00:33:44,399
Aah!

528
00:33:44,524 --> 00:33:45,734
Shit!

529
00:33:48,028 --> 00:33:49,946
Is somebody there?

530
00:33:50,030 --> 00:33:52,615
Hello?

531
00:33:54,117 --> 00:33:55,452
Hello?

532
00:35:10,193 --> 00:35:11,653
Oh, my God!

533
00:35:13,446 --> 00:35:15,198
Let go!
What are you doing?

534
00:35:15,448 --> 00:35:16,700
[Subway Horn
Blows]

535
00:35:16,825 --> 00:35:18,034
Aah!

536
00:35:20,537 --> 00:35:22,414
Like trains?

537
00:35:32,674 --> 00:35:35,051
Stay out! This is mine!

538
00:35:37,303 --> 00:35:39,723
[Horn Blows]

539
00:36:52,170 --> 00:36:54,005
Shit.

540
00:36:57,175 --> 00:36:58,718
[Dialing Telephone]

541
00:37:04,307 --> 00:37:06,768
It's me.
I couldn't get it.

542
00:37:06,851 --> 00:37:09,187
She came home.

543
00:37:09,312 --> 00:37:11,773
Give me a couple
of days, man.

544
00:37:11,856 --> 00:37:13,274
I'll go back.

545
00:37:13,358 --> 00:37:15,068
Relax.

546
00:37:15,193 --> 00:37:16,653
I'll get it.

547
00:37:18,113 --> 00:37:19,614
Get what?

548
00:37:22,158 --> 00:37:23,618
Who are you?

549
00:37:23,702 --> 00:37:25,995
What do you
want from us?

550
00:37:30,709 --> 00:37:32,002
No.

551
00:37:32,127 --> 00:37:36,047
You stay away
from her.

552
00:37:36,131 --> 00:37:37,590
Do you hear me?

553
00:37:37,716 --> 00:37:40,844
Stay away from her!

554
00:37:43,179 --> 00:37:45,181
[Gospel Music Playing]

555
00:38:04,117 --> 00:38:05,243
And...

556
00:38:05,368 --> 00:38:08,079
teddy bear, teddy bear,
turn around,

557
00:38:08,246 --> 00:38:09,664
teddy bear,
teddy bear,

558
00:38:09,831 --> 00:38:11,624
touch
the ground.

559
00:38:42,447 --> 00:38:44,157
Rosa Santiago?

560
00:38:50,330 --> 00:38:51,706
Please
be seated.

561
00:39:07,472 --> 00:39:10,392
Our sister will be
with us soon.

562
00:39:12,727 --> 00:39:15,230
Sister Oda Mae,

563
00:39:15,397 --> 00:39:19,359
grant us the gift of
your all-seeing presence.

564
00:39:19,484 --> 00:39:22,153
Appear before us
now.

565
00:39:27,826 --> 00:39:29,828
Mrs. Santiago?

566
00:39:30,036 --> 00:39:31,955
Buenos dias.

567
