it happens sometimes

834
00:51:42,727 --> 00:51:45,021
that the spirit gets
yanked out so quick

835
00:51:45,105 --> 00:51:46,606
that the essence
still feels

836
00:51:46,731 --> 00:51:48,024
it has work to do.

837
00:51:48,108 --> 00:51:49,526
Would you stop rambling?

838
00:51:49,651 --> 00:51:50,944
I'm just answering
her question.

839
00:51:51,069 --> 00:51:52,529
He's got
an attitude now.

840
00:51:52,654 --> 00:51:54,656
I don't have an attitude.

841
00:51:54,781 --> 00:51:56,700
Yes, you do
have an attitude.

842
00:51:56,783 --> 00:51:58,034
We're having
a little discussion.

843
00:51:58,159 --> 00:51:59,953
If you didn't have
a attitude,

844
00:52:00,078 --> 00:52:01,830
you wouldn't have
raised your voice.

845
00:52:01,913 --> 00:52:03,415
God damn it,
Oda Mae--

846
00:52:03,581 --> 00:52:04,833
Don't you god damn me.

847
00:52:04,958 --> 00:52:07,168
Don't you take
the Lord's name in vain.

848
00:52:07,252 --> 00:52:08,628
Would you relax?

849
00:52:08,753 --> 00:52:10,630
You relax.
You're the dead guy.

850
00:52:10,755 --> 00:52:12,632
Want me to help?
You apologize.

851
00:52:12,757 --> 00:52:13,633
Jesus Christ!

852
00:52:13,758 --> 00:52:14,801
I'm leaving.

853
00:52:14,926 --> 00:52:17,220
Nobody talks to me like that,
you understand?

854
00:52:17,262 --> 00:52:18,763
Now, you better
apologize.

855
00:52:18,888 --> 00:52:20,223
I'm sorry.

856
00:52:20,265 --> 00:52:21,224
I apologize.

857
00:52:21,266 --> 00:52:22,851
OK?

858
00:52:22,934 --> 00:52:25,729
Now, would you
sit down?

859
00:52:25,812 --> 00:52:26,730
Please?

860
00:52:26,813 --> 00:52:28,940
He's apologized.

861
00:52:30,150 --> 00:52:33,069
I need you to tell
Molly what I'm saying,

862
00:52:33,153 --> 00:52:36,072
but you have to tell her
word for word.

863
00:52:36,197 --> 00:52:39,659
Yes. He wants me to tell you
what he's saying

864
00:52:39,784 --> 00:52:41,870
word for word.

865
00:52:46,833 --> 00:52:48,126
Molly, you're in danger.

866
00:52:48,251 --> 00:52:51,129
You can't just
blurt it out like that.

867
00:52:51,254 --> 00:52:52,922
And quit moving around,
will you?

868
00:52:53,048 --> 00:52:54,549
You're making me dizzy.

869
00:52:54,632 --> 00:52:57,052
I'll just tell her
in my own way.

870
00:52:57,177 --> 00:53:00,680
Molly, you in danger,
girl.

871
00:53:00,805 --> 00:53:02,724
What are you
talking about?

872
00:53:02,807 --> 00:53:04,893
I know the man
who killed me.

873
00:53:04,976 --> 00:53:06,519
He knows
who killed him.

874
00:53:06,644 --> 00:53:09,189
His name's Willy Lopez.
I know where he lives.

875
00:53:09,314 --> 00:53:11,232
He's a Puerto Rican,
Willy Lopez.

876
00:53:11,316 --> 00:53:12,776
He knows
where he lives.

877
00:53:12,817 --> 00:53:13,777
Write it down.

878
00:53:13,818 --> 00:53:15,153
You write it down.

879
00:53:15,278 --> 00:53:16,738
I ain't no
damn secretary.

880
00:53:16,821 --> 00:53:17,781
Just do it!

881
00:53:17,864 --> 00:53:19,199
Argh!

882
00:53:19,324 --> 00:53:21,743
He's so testy.

883
00:53:21,826 --> 00:53:24,788
What is it you
want me to write?

884
00:53:24,871 --> 00:53:27,665
It's 303 Prospect Place,
apartment 4-D.

885
00:53:27,791 --> 00:53:29,125
303 Prospect Place?

886
00:53:29,167 --> 00:53:30,126
Yeah.

887
00:53:30,210 --> 00:53:32,253
That's my
neighborhood.

888
00:53:32,337 --> 00:53:34,297
Molly, he's got
my wallet,

889
00:53:34,339 --> 00:53:35,840
he's got my key,

890
00:53:35,965 --> 00:53:37,300
and he was
in here.

891
00:53:37,342 --> 00:53:40,720
He's got his wallet
and key and was here.

892
00:53:40,845 --> 00:53:42,722
Yesterday after your
walk with Carl,

893
00:53:42,847 --> 00:53:45,141
you talked to Floyd,
took off your clothes--

894
00:53:45,266 --> 00:53:46,726
All right,
all right.

895
00:53:46,851 --> 00:53:49,062
When you came in
after your walk with Carl,

896
00:53:49,187 --> 00:53:51,106
he saw
everything.

897
00:53:51,189 --> 00:53:53,650
Go to the police.
It was a setup.

898
00:53:53,775 --> 00:53:55,694
I was murdered.

899
00:53:55,819 --> 00:53:58,780
He says go to the police.
He was murdered.

900
00:53:58,863 --> 00:54:00,115
There's somebody
else involved--

901
00:54:00,198 --> 00:54:02,992
I don't want no more
to do with this.

902
00:54:03,118 --> 00:54:04,619
Where are you going?

903
00:54:04,703 --> 00:54:07,664
I'm leaving, I did everything
I said I'd do.

904
00:54:07,706 --> 00:54:09,791
And don't be
following me.

905
00:54:09,874 --> 00:54:11,793
I'm finished.
I mean it.

906
00:54:11,876 --> 00:54:14,170
Have a nice life.
Have a nice death.

907
00:54:14,295 --> 00:54:15,296
Goodbye.

908
00:54:18,008 --> 00:54:20,343
Molly, there is no one
on earth besides you

909
00:54:20,635 --> 00:54:23,763
who wants this
to be true more than me,

910
00:54:23,888 --> 00:54:26,141
but you got to be
rational about this.

911
00:54:26,224 --> 00:54:29,310
Sam is no more
in this room than--

912
00:54:29,394 --> 00:54:34,983
Look, I understand the
need to hang on to him,

913
00:54:35,108 --> 00:54:38,069
I really do,
but this is absurd.

914
00:54:38,194 --> 00:54:42,157
I know this seems absurd,
but it had to be real.

915
00:54:42,282 --> 00:54:44,200
You believed some
fortune-teller from Brooklyn

916
00:54:44,284 --> 00:54:46,286
who shows up
at your door?

917
00:54:46,411 --> 00:54:49,289
I watched her have
a conversation with him.

918
00:54:49,414 --> 00:54:51,666
I don't buy it, Moll,
not for a minute.

919
00:54:51,791 --> 00:54:53,960
What about the things
she knew?

920
00:54:54,085 --> 00:54:55,670
What things?

921
00:54:55,795 --> 00:54:59,382
The photo Sam took of me
on our trip to Reno.

922
00:54:59,674 --> 00:55:01,259
Carl, we were alone.

923
00:55:01,384 --> 00:55:04,846
And the green underwear
that I wrote my name in.

924
00:55:08,058 --> 00:55:10,602
She said Sam knew
who killed him.

925
00:55:10,769 --> 00:55:14,022
Yeah, that he
was set up.

926
00:55:14,064 --> 00:55:16,066
This is getting
deranged.

927
00:55:16,107 --> 00:55:17,609
We're off
the deep end.

928
00:55:17,734 --> 00:55:19,903
She had a name
and an address--

929
00:55:19,944 --> 00:55:20,904
Willy Lopez.

930
00:55:20,945 --> 00:55:23,281
303 Prospect Place,
apartment 4-D.

931
00:55:24,824 --> 00:55:26,159
This is sick.

932
00:55:26,284 --> 00:55:27,744
Oh, Carl.

933
00:55:27,911 --> 00:55:29,829
This is really sick.

934
00:55:30,955 --> 00:55:31,915
Oh, God.

935
00:55:32,040 --> 00:55:33,375
Molly, I don't
understand

936
00:55:33,458 --> 00:55:35,377
how you could--
you could...

937
00:55:38,046 --> 00:55:39,923
swallow this crap.
I mean...

938
00:55:40,048 --> 00:55:42,384
this guy
may not even exist.

939
00:55:42,467 --> 00:55:45,428
Maybe she's just
trying to use you

940
00:55:45,512 --> 00:55:48,056
to set someone up.

941
00:55:48,223 --> 00:55:50,183
You're right.

942
00:55:50,308 --> 00:55:51,768
You're absolutely right.

943
00:55:51,893 --> 00:55:54,771
That's what
I got to find out.

944
00:55:54,896 --> 00:55:57,232
What do you mean,
find out?

945
00:55:57,357 --> 00:56:00,402
She said Sam wants me
to go to the police.

946
00:56:00,735 --> 00:56:03,071
Sam wants you to
go to the police?

947
00:56:03,154 --> 00:56:05,949
Jesus, Moll. Are you
out of your mind?

948
00:56:05,990 --> 00:56:08,326
What are you going
to tell the police?

949
00:56:08,451 --> 00:56:09,911
That some
storefront psychic

950
00:56:09,994 --> 00:56:12,330
has been communing
with the dead?

951
00:56:12,455 --> 00:56:14,916
Do you know what
that sounds like?

952
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:17,335
You're talking ghosts here,
for Christ's sake.

953
00:56:19,129 --> 00:56:20,046
I'm sorry.

954
00:56:20,130 --> 00:56:22,924
This stuff just really
gets to me,

955
00:56:23,008 --> 00:56:23,925
you know?

956
00:56:24,009 --> 00:56:26,302
It's OK if you
don't believe me.

957
00:56:26,428 --> 00:56:27,929
I'm trying to, Molly.

958
00:56:31,516 --> 00:56:33,101
Look...

959
00:56:33,226 --> 00:56:36,146
if it'll make you
feel any better,

960
00:56:36,229 --> 00:56:40,358
I'll go check
this out, OK?

961
00:56:40,483 --> 00:56:43,361
I want you to try
and get some sleep.

962
00:56:43,486 --> 00:56:44,362
OK?

963
00:56:44,487 --> 00:56:46,322
All right.

964
00:56:47,490 --> 00:56:49,367
I'll call you
in the morning.

965
00:56:49,492 --> 00:56:50,368
OK.

966
00:57:18,396 --> 00:57:19,481
Be careful.

967
00:57:29,908 --> 00:57:31,785
[Knock Knock]

968
00:57:33,411 --> 00:57:34,329
Carl.

969
00:57:34,412 --> 00:57:37,332
What the hell
are you doing here?

970
00:57:38,625 --> 00:57:40,543
Who you been
talking to, Willy?

971
00:57:40,627 --> 00:57:43,046
''Talking to''?
What the hell do you mean?

972
00:57:43,213 --> 00:57:45,382
Some woman knows
all about you, everything.

973
00:57:45,465 --> 00:57:47,384
Where's she
getting it from?

974
00:57:47,467 --> 00:57:49,969
I haven't said
a word to anybody.

975
00:57:50,095 --> 00:57:52,389
She knows your name
and where you live.

976
00:57:52,472 --> 00:57:54,933
A lot of women
know where I live.

977
00:57:55,058 --> 00:57:56,935
This is not a joke.

978
00:57:57,060 --> 00:57:58,978
She knows
about the murder.

979
00:57:59,104 --> 00:58:01,398
I want you
to find this bitch,

980
00:58:01,481 --> 00:58:02,982
whoever she is,

981
00:58:03,108 --> 00:58:04,984
and I want you to--

982
00:58:06,945 --> 00:58:09,239
Just get rid
of her, OK?

983
00:58:09,322 --> 00:58:13,827
I've got $4 million stuck
in a god damn computer.

984
00:58:13,952 --> 00:58:16,246
If I don't get
those codes,

985
00:58:16,371 --> 00:58:19,249
if that money is not
transferred soon...

986
00:58:21,960 --> 00:58:23,461
I'm...

987
00:58:23,586 --> 00:58:24,546
dead.

988
00:58:24,629 --> 00:58:26,131
We're both dead.

989
00:58:26,256 --> 00:58:28,508
Why not tell them
you only launder money

990
00:58:28,633 --> 00:58:30,093
the first of the month?

991
00:58:30,176 --> 00:58:32,012
What the hell
is wrong with you?

992
00:58:32,137 --> 00:58:34,472
Is everything a joke?

993
00:58:34,639 --> 00:58:36,266
You killed a man.

994
00:58:36,433 --> 00:58:37,392
You were supposed
to steal his wallet.

995
00:58:37,559 --> 00:58:39,978
-Was that a joke?
-I did you a favor.

996
00:58:40,103 --> 00:58:41,438
That was a freebie.

997
00:58:42,647 --> 00:58:45,859
Look, these are
drug dealers, OK?

998
00:58:45,984 --> 00:58:48,319
Just don't blow this
for me.

999
00:58:48,403 --> 00:58:51,281
I've risked my job.
I could go to jail.

1000
00:58:51,364 --> 00:58:54,534
$80,000 of that money
is mine.

1001
00:58:57,912 --> 00:58:59,122
Look, just...

1002
00:58:59,247 --> 00:59:01,916
let me have the key
to Sam's apartment.

1003
00:59:02,000 --> 00:59:04,586
I'll get the address book
myself, OK?

1004
00:59:30,487 --> 00:59:32,947
You god damn bastard!

1005
00:59:33,031 --> 00:59:34,032
Why?

1006
00:59:34,157 --> 00:59:36,576
Why? You were
my friend!

1007
00:59:38,995 --> 00:59:41,331
I had a life,
god damn you.

1008
00:59:41,498 --> 00:59:43,166
I had a life!

1009
00:59:52,217 --> 00:59:55,470
Look, I don't even believe
in this stuff myself.

1010
00:59:55,553 --> 00:59:57,013
But she was real.

1011
00:59:57,138 --> 01:00:00,725
You think I'd come down here
if it wasn't real?

1012
01:00:02,143 --> 01:00:02,727
You know,

1013
01:00:03,186 --> 01:00:06,481
you told me if I had
any new information

1014
01:00:06,564 --> 01:00:08,066
that I should come.

1015
01:00:08,149 --> 01:00:09,484
So here I am.

1016
01:00:13,655 --> 01:00:15,573
I know
how this sounds.

1017
01:00:15,657 --> 01:00:17,575
I hear myself
saying it,

1018
01:00:17,659 --> 01:00:19,577
and I want
to cringe.

1019
01:00:19,661 --> 01:00:22,622
But this woman knew things
she couldn't have known.

1020
01:00:22,706 --> 01:00:25,166
Things Sam
only said to me.

1021
01:00:25,333 --> 01:00:28,336
OK, according to this
psychic lady,

1022
01:00:28,461 --> 01:00:32,799
there are ghosts and spirits
all over the place

1023
01:00:33,049 --> 01:00:34,801
watching us
all the time?

1024
01:00:35,051 --> 01:00:35,802
Huh?

1025
01:00:38,555 --> 01:00:41,516
Hell, I'm never going
to get undressed again.

1026
01:00:41,558 --> 01:00:42,517
Excuse me.

1027
01:00:42,559 --> 01:00:45,520
I got more
important things to do.

1028
01:00:56,406 --> 01:00:58,700
The guy's name
is Willy Lopez.

1029
01:00:58,825 --> 01:01:02,162
All I'm asking you to do
is check it out.

1030
01:01:02,287 --> 01:01:03,621
OK. Wait here.

1031
01:01:03,705 --> 01:01:07,417
Let me see if the guy's
got a record, all right?

1032
01:01:07,542 --> 01:01:09,252
Great.

1033
01:02:11,773 --> 01:02:13,316
What are you doing?

1034
01:02:13,441 --> 01:02:15,443
Where's the file
on Willy Lopez?

1035
01:02:15,568 --> 01:02:17,070
There isn't one.

1036
01:02:17,153 --> 01:02:19,072
He was probably
some old boyfriend

1037
01:02:19,155 --> 01:02:21,491
she was trying
to get even with.

1038
01:02:21,574 --> 01:02:23,493
This psychic woman's
got a record

1039
01:02:23,576 --> 01:02:26,079
that goes back
a long way.

1040
01:02:26,204 --> 01:02:27,080
1 967,

1041
01:02:27,205 --> 01:02:28,665
Shreveport,

1042
01:02:28,790 --> 01:02:29,791
forgery...

1043
01:02:30,125 --> 01:02:32,460
selling false I.D.

1044
01:02:32,585 --> 01:02:35,213
Served one year, 1 9 7 1 .

1045
01:02:35,338 --> 01:02:38,174
Baton Rouge,
arrested for fraud.

1046
01:02:38,341 --> 01:02:42,387
Numbers racketeering,
served 1 0 months, 1 9 7 4.

1047
01:02:42,512 --> 01:02:43,930
Look,
this is impossible.

1048
01:02:44,180 --> 01:02:46,349
It goes on and on.

1049
01:02:46,474 --> 01:02:48,351
She knew things,
private things.

1050
01:02:48,476 --> 01:02:50,854
Now, how could she
have known all that?

1051
01:02:50,979 --> 01:02:53,481
A lot of times
they read the obits.

1052
01:02:53,523 --> 01:02:56,818
She just had to see
the word ''banker''--boom.

1053
01:02:56,860 --> 01:02:59,320
Hell, they even go
through your...garbage

1054
01:02:59,404 --> 01:03:01,406
to find things
they can use--

1055
01:03:01,531 --> 01:03:02,866
letters, old papers.

1056
01:03:03,116 --> 01:03:04,451
It doesn't take much.

1057
01:03:05,535 --> 01:03:06,453
No.

1058
01:03:08,663 --> 01:03:10,165
It was real.

1059
01:03:12,876 --> 01:03:14,836
She knew about a...

1060
01:03:15,170 --> 01:03:16,463
a sweater I knitted.

1061
01:03:18,590 --> 01:03:19,883
And songs we sang.

1062
01:03:24,888 --> 01:03:27,182
Our trip
to Montego Bay.

1063
01:03:29,684 --> 01:03:30,727
I'm sorry.

1064
01:03:30,894 --> 01:03:33,355
I know this is hard.

1065
01:03:33,438 --> 01:03:35,774
People want so much
to believe.

1066
01:03:35,899 --> 01:03:36,775
They're grieving,

1067
01:03:36,900 --> 01:03:38,234
they're vulnerable...

1068
01:03:39,569 --> 01:03:41,696
and they will
give anything

1069
01:03:41,821 --> 01:03:43,323
for one last moment.

1070
01:03:43,406 --> 01:03:44,741
Believe me.

1071
01:03:44,866 --> 01:03:47,660
These people know
what they're doing.

1072
01:03:47,744 --> 01:03:50,205
I know
how you must feel,

1073
01:03:50,330 --> 01:03:53,249
but you know
you can press charges.

1074
01:03:56,920 --> 01:03:57,921
No.

1075
01:04:01,841 --> 01:04:02,759
Thank you.

1076
01:04:17,440 --> 01:04:19,693
Oh, God,
let this be it.

1077
01:04:32,455 --> 01:04:33,373
Yes.

1078
01:04:43,967 --> 01:04:45,510
[Ring]

1079
01:04:45,635 --> 01:04:46,594
Hello.

1080
01:04:46,636 --> 01:04:47,971
Eddie? It's Carl Bruner.

1081
01:04:48,263 --> 01:04:48,972
What's up?

1082
01:04:49,264 --> 01:04:49,973
Everything's fine.

1083
01:04:50,306 --> 01:04:51,599
Just, we're all set.

1084
01:04:51,683 --> 01:04:54,561
Let me know what
you want me to do.

1085
01:04:54,644 --> 01:04:56,563
Want you to
transfer the money

1086
01:04:56,646 --> 01:04:57,981
from the 1 2
separate accounts

1087
01:04:58,064 --> 01:04:59,107
into a single account
under the name Rita Miller.

1088
01:05:00,525 --> 01:05:01,860
OK.

1089
01:05:01,943 --> 01:05:03,862
Tomorrow at five minutes
before closing,

1090
01:05:03,945 --> 01:05:05,780
3:55 p.m.,

1091
01:05:05,864 --> 01:05:09,784
transfer the full account to
the First Island Bank of Nassau,

1092
01:05:09,868 --> 01:05:12,579
registry number
486-9580.

1093
01:05:12,704 --> 01:05:14,622
Call us when it's done.

1094
01:05:14,706 --> 01:05:16,207
OK. I've got it.

1095
01:05:16,291 --> 01:05:17,709
Just tell Mr. Balistrari

1096
01:05:17,834 --> 01:05:20,628
that there won't be
any more problems, OK?

1097
01:05:20,712 --> 01:05:22,213
Yeah. I'll do that.

1098
01:05:22,297 --> 01:05:23,214
Thank you.

1099
01:05:23,340 --> 01:05:24,632
Good work, Carl.

1100
01:06:24,109 --> 01:06:26,611
Molly, why
can't you hear me?

1101
01:06:26,695 --> 01:06:28,321
I need you.

1102
01:06:29,614 --> 01:06:31,366
[Knock On Door]

1103
01:06:32,909 --> 01:06:34,828
[Knock Knock Knock]

1104
01:06:40,542 --> 01:06:41,876
Who is it?

1105
01:06:41,918 --> 01:06:43,420
It's Carl, Molly.

1106
01:06:43,545 --> 01:06:44,504
No.

1107
01:06:44,629 --> 01:06:45,922
Don't open it,
Molly.

1108
01:06:46,047 --> 01:06:47,549
He's a murderer.

1109
01:06:47,632 --> 01:06:48,550
Hi.

1110
01:06:48,633 --> 01:06:49,551
Hey.

1111
01:06:49,634 --> 01:06:50,927
I know it's late.

1112
01:06:51,052 --> 01:06:52,804
I'm sorry
to disturb you.

1113
01:06:52,929 --> 01:06:55,473
I've been thinking
about you all day,

1114
01:06:55,598 --> 01:06:58,893
and I feel really lousy
about what happened last night.

1115
01:06:58,935 --> 01:07:00,311
This supernatural
thing just--

1116
01:07:00,437 --> 01:07:02,480
Don't worry about it.
It's OK.

1117
01:07:02,605 --> 01:07:03,732
No, it's not.

1118
01:07:03,857 --> 01:07:06,776
You needed me to hear you,
and I didn't.

1119
01:07:06,901 --> 01:07:09,779
I wasn't there for you,
and that was...

1120
01:07:09,904 --> 01:07:11,531
that was wrong.

1121
01:07:11,656 --> 01:07:12,949
It's just, I...

1122
01:07:14,617 --> 01:07:15,952
I just--

1123
01:07:16,036 --> 01:07:18,997
I want you to know
that I'm your friend.

1124
01:07:19,080 --> 01:07:20,582
Thanks, Carl.

1125
01:07:20,707 --> 01:07:22,542
You were never
our friend.

1126
01:07:22,625 --> 01:07:24,961
That really means
a lot to me.

1127
01:07:25,086 --> 01:07:27,714
Me, too. I brought you
some Japanese apple pears.

1128
01:07:27,839 --> 01:07:29,341
I know you like them.

1129
01:07:31,092 --> 01:07:31,968
Thanks.

1130
01:07:32,093 --> 01:07:33,553
That's very sweet.

1131
01:07:33,678 --> 01:07:35,847
Could I come in
for a second?

1132
01:07:35,972 --> 01:07:38,391
It's just been
one of those days.

1133
01:07:38,475 --> 01:07:39,642
Maybe some coffee?

1134
01:07:39,809 --> 01:07:40,977
Yeah. Come on in.

1135
01:07:41,144 --> 01:07:42,771
No, Molly.

1136
01:07:42,896 --> 01:07:44,814
You seem a little tense.

1137
01:07:44,898 --> 01:07:46,399
Are you OK?

1138
01:07:46,483 --> 01:07:47,817
No. I'm fine.

1139
01:07:47,942 --> 01:07:50,820
It's just--
What can I tell you?

1140
01:07:50,945 --> 01:07:52,447
It's been tough.

1141
01:07:52,489 --> 01:07:54,741
It just still hurts
so much.

1142
01:07:54,824 --> 01:07:56,159
You lying snake.

1143
01:07:56,242 --> 01:07:59,120
And on top of it,
it's stuff at work.

1144
01:07:59,371 --> 01:08:01,456
They've given me
my own accounts,

1145
01:08:01,581 --> 01:08:02,874
which is good,

1146
01:08:02,999 --> 01:08:06,461
but I just haven't really
had time to adjust,

1147
01:08:06,586 --> 01:08:08,380
kind of absorb
everything.

1148
01:08:12,676 --> 01:08:13,927
It's no big deal.

1149
01:08:16,930 --> 01:08:17,847
Yeah.

1150
01:08:24,187 --> 01:08:27,148
Can I have just
a little more cream?

1151
01:08:28,191 --> 01:08:29,401
Yeah.

1152
01:08:30,819 --> 01:08:31,861
Oh, shit.

1153
01:08:32,028 --> 01:08:34,489
Jesus. I can't believe
I did that.

1154
01:08:34,572 --> 01:08:35,782
Are you all right?

1155
01:08:35,865 --> 01:08:37,826
Yeah, I'm fine.

1156
01:08:37,867 --> 01:08:38,785
Oh, God.

1157
01:08:38,868 --> 01:08:41,162
Let me throw that
in the washer.

1158
01:08:41,246 --> 01:08:44,040
Don't worry about it.
It's OK. It's just...

1159
01:08:44,207 --> 01:08:45,667
You want
another shirt?

1160
01:08:45,750 --> 01:08:48,211
No. It'll dry.
It'll just take a minute.

1161
01:08:48,294 --> 01:08:49,754
There you go.

1162
01:08:53,008 --> 01:08:54,259
Where were you today?

1163
01:08:54,551 --> 01:08:57,554
I thought you were going
to come into the bank

1164
01:08:57,679 --> 01:08:59,014
and sign those papers?

1165
01:08:59,097 --> 01:09:01,766
I was supposed to,
but I didn't have time.

1166
01:09:01,891 --> 01:09:04,853
I went to the police.

1167
01:09:11,234 --> 01:09:12,193
You did?

1168
01:09:12,527 --> 01:09:14,404
Wow. What
did you tell them?

1169
01:09:14,529 --> 01:09:15,822
What did they say?

1170
01:09:15,905 --> 01:09:17,407
It was awful.

1171
01:09:18,742 --> 01:09:20,618
I felt really stupid.

1172
01:09:20,744 --> 01:09:24,039
They brought out a file
on this woman and--

1173
01:09:24,080 --> 01:09:26,041
At least
1 0 inches thick.

1174
01:09:27,167 --> 01:09:28,752
A ripoff artist, huh?

1175
01:09:28,877 --> 01:09:29,919
No, Molly.

1176
01:09:31,755 --> 01:09:33,631
You know,
the sad thing...

1177
01:09:35,258 --> 01:09:37,218
is that
I believed her.

1178
01:09:37,302 --> 01:09:38,762
Molly...

1179
01:09:40,847 --> 01:09:42,891
sometimes
we need to believe.

1180
01:09:44,517 --> 01:09:45,852
Why? What's the point?

1181
01:09:45,935 --> 01:09:47,312
Molly, it's not easy to face
the realities of life sometimes.

1182
01:09:49,773 --> 01:09:51,816
You got to
give yourself that.

1183
01:09:51,941 --> 01:09:56,654
What you've got to remember
is the love that you guys felt.

1184
01:09:56,780 --> 01:09:59,115
You got to remember
how good Sam was.

1185
01:09:59,157 --> 01:10:01,659
You were everything
to him, Molly.

1186
01:10:01,785 --> 01:10:03,119
You were his life.

1187
01:10:17,884 --> 01:10:19,219
I feel so alone.

1188
01:10:27,936 --> 01:10:29,270
You're not alone.

1189
01:10:29,354 --> 01:10:30,271
OK?

1190
01:10:31,648 --> 01:10:34,025
You got your work.
You're incredibly talented.

1191
01:10:34,150 --> 01:10:35,068
You're young.

1192
01:10:35,151 --> 01:10:37,362
You're fantastically
gorgeous.

1193
01:10:39,072 --> 01:10:41,408
I don't know
what's real anymore.

1194
01:10:42,659 --> 01:10:45,161
I don't know
what to think.

1195
01:10:48,373 --> 01:10:50,083
Just think about Sam.

1196
01:10:52,752 --> 01:10:55,630
Think about the time
you guys had together.

1197
01:10:56,840 --> 01:10:58,675
How wonderful that was.

1198
01:10:59,926 --> 01:11:01,052
Yeah.

1199
01:11:02,262 --> 01:11:05,181
Let your feelings out,
Moll. It's OK.

1200
01:11:05,348 --> 01:11:07,767
Life turns on a dime.

1201
01:11:09,269 --> 01:11:10,270
You know?

1202
01:11:11,980 --> 01:11:12,981
I mean...

1203
01:11:14,107 --> 01:11:15,650
people think that...

1204
01:11:15,775 --> 01:11:18,820
they're there forever, that there's
always going to be tomorrow,

1205
01:11:18,945 --> 01:11:20,238
but that's bullshit.

1206
01:11:20,363 --> 01:11:22,323
Sam taught us that.

1207
01:11:23,825 --> 01:11:26,161
You have to
live for now.

1208
01:11:28,788 --> 01:11:29,914
For today.

1209
01:11:50,018 --> 01:11:50,894
I can't.

1210
01:11:51,019 --> 01:11:51,895
I'm sorry.

1211
01:11:52,020 --> 01:11:52,896
It's OK.

1212
01:11:53,063 --> 01:11:55,732
I--I--I can't.
It's just too soon.

1213
01:11:55,815 --> 01:11:56,733
It's OK.

1214
01:11:56,816 --> 01:11:58,735
You've been great,
Carl.

1215
01:12:01,738 --> 01:12:03,698
But I need you
to leave.

1216
01:12:03,740 --> 01:12:05,075
I understand totally.

1217
01:12:05,200 --> 01:12:06,076
Please.

1218
01:12:11,790 --> 01:12:15,001
Could we just have dinner
tomorrow night? Just talk?

1219
01:12:15,085 --> 01:12:17,420
Can I interest you
in that?

1220
01:12:18,797 --> 01:12:19,839
Yeah.

1221
01:12:19,923 --> 01:12:20,840
Sure.

1222
01:12:20,924 --> 01:12:21,841
Great.

1223
01:13:30,160 --> 01:13:31,036
Hey.

1224
01:13:35,790 --> 01:13:38,126
Get off my train!

1225
01:13:38,209 --> 01:13:39,127
No.

1226
01:13:39,210 --> 01:13:41,004
Get off!

1227
01:13:41,046 --> 01:13:42,088
Get off!

1228
01:13:42,172 --> 01:13:43,006
Get off!

1229
01:13:43,048 --> 01:13:44,341
Get off!

1230
01:13:44,466 --> 01:13:45,842
Get off!

1231
01:13:45,925 --> 01:13:47,052
Get out of here!

1232
01:13:47,177 --> 01:13:48,178
Get off!

1233
01:13:48,345 --> 01:13:49,220
No.

1234
01:13:49,346 --> 01:13:51,222
Show me
how you do that.

1235
01:13:51,348 --> 01:13:53,558
I'm not leaving
till you teach me.

1236
01:13:53,850 --> 01:13:54,809
Get off!

1237
01:13:54,934 --> 01:13:55,977
No.

1238
01:13:56,061 --> 01:13:56,978
Get off!

1239
01:14:04,027 --> 01:14:06,488
You stubborn asshole.

1240
01:14:06,571 --> 01:14:08,073
Ha ha ha.

1241
01:14:08,198 --> 01:14:09,532
What are you doing?

1242
01:14:09,574 --> 01:14:11,534
What the hell
are you doing?

1243
01:14:11,576 --> 01:14:13,078
What am I doing?

1244
01:14:13,203 --> 01:14:15,538
You're trying to move it
with your finger.

1245
01:14:15,580 --> 01:14:17,916
You can't push it.
You're dead.

1246
01:14:26,424 --> 01:14:28,385
It's all in your mind.

1247
01:14:28,426 --> 01:14:31,930
The problem with you
is you still think you're real.

1248
01:14:32,055 --> 01:14:33,932
You think you're
wearing those clothes?

1249
01:14:34,057 --> 01:14:36,267
You think you're crouched
on that floor?

1250
01:14:36,393 --> 01:14:37,268
Bullshit!

1251
01:14:37,394 --> 01:14:39,854
You ain't got a body
no more, son!

1252
01:14:39,979 --> 01:14:41,314
It's all up here!

1253
01:14:41,398 --> 01:14:42,899
You want
to move something,

1254
01:14:42,982 --> 01:14:45,318
you got to move it
with your mind!

1255
01:14:45,402 --> 01:14:46,903
You got to focus!

1256
01:14:46,986 --> 01:14:48,905
How? How do you focus?

1257
01:14:48,988 --> 01:14:51,408
I don't know
how you focus.

1258
01:14:51,533 --> 01:14:53,034
You just focus.

1259
01:14:56,329 --> 01:14:58,081
How did you do that?

1260
01:14:58,164 --> 01:15:00,417
You got to take
all your emotions,

1261
01:15:00,458 --> 01:15:03,211
all your anger, all your love,
all your hate,

1262
01:15:03,253 --> 01:15:04,587
and push it way down

1263
01:15:04,879 --> 01:15:06,464
into the pit
of your stomach

1264
01:15:06,589 --> 01:15:09,050
and let it explode
like a reactor. Pow!

1265
01:15:11,302 --> 01:15:12,262
OK.

1266
01:15:12,345 --> 01:15:13,263
OK.

1267
01:15:18,268 --> 01:15:19,853
Don't laugh.

1268
01:15:44,586 --> 01:15:46,129
Way to go, kid.

1269
01:15:46,296 --> 01:15:47,630
I did it.

1270
01:15:49,382 --> 01:15:50,925
I did it.

1271
01:15:51,051 --> 01:15:52,344
Way to go.

1272
01:15:59,351 --> 01:16:02,228
From your gut,
like I told you.

1273
01:16:05,190 --> 01:16:08,151
Give it time.
What else have you got?

1274
01:16:15,658 --> 01:16:18,119
How long
have you been here?

1275
01:16:20,330 --> 01:16:22,457
Since they pushed me.

1276
01:16:22,624 --> 01:16:24,125
Someone pushed you?

1277
01:16:24,209 --> 01:16:25,460
Yeah, someone pushed me.

1278
01:16:25,543 --> 01:16:26,961
Who?

1279
01:16:27,045 --> 01:16:28,338
You don't believe me?

1280
01:16:28,463 --> 01:16:31,341
You think I fell?
You think I jumped?

1281
01:16:31,424 --> 01:16:32,884
Well, fuck you!

1282
01:16:33,009 --> 01:16:34,511
It wasn't my time!

1283
01:16:34,678 --> 01:16:36,554
I wasn't supposed to go!

1284
01:16:36,680 --> 01:16:39,140
I'm not supposed
to be here!

1285
01:16:41,685 --> 01:16:43,353
Oh.

1286
01:16:44,729 --> 01:16:45,939
Oh.

1287
01:16:48,274 --> 01:16:52,404
Oh, I'd give anything
for a drag.

1288
01:16:52,529 --> 01:16:54,698
Just one drag.

1289
01:16:55,031 --> 01:16:56,574
Are you all right?

1290
01:16:56,700 --> 01:16:59,327
Who are you?
Why are you hounding me?

1291
01:16:59,452 --> 01:17:01,413
Who sent you?

1292
01:17:03,498 --> 01:17:05,291
Who sent you?

1293
01:17:07,460 --> 01:17:09,004
Leave me alone.

1294
01:17:09,129 --> 01:17:10,463
Leave me alone!

1295
01:17:10,547 --> 01:17:12,674
Leave me alone!

1296
01:17:56,259 --> 01:17:57,260
Yes!

1297
01:18:12,609 --> 01:18:14,110
You need
to concentrate,

1298
01:18:14,194 --> 01:18:15,528
'cause if
you concentrate,

1299
01:18:15,612 --> 01:18:17,113
you'll probably
rouse him.

1300
01:18:17,197 --> 01:18:18,531
What's his name
again?

1301
01:18:18,615 --> 01:18:19,532
Orlando.

1302
01:18:19,616 --> 01:18:20,617
Orlando.

1303
01:18:20,742 --> 01:18:23,578
Orlando. Orlando.
Is there an Orlando here?

1304
01:18:23,661 --> 01:18:24,579
I'm here.

1305
01:18:24,662 --> 01:18:25,580
He's here.

1306
01:18:25,663 --> 01:18:26,998
Oda Mae, I--

1307
01:18:27,123 --> 01:18:27,999
Sam.

1308
01:18:28,124 --> 01:18:29,459
Excuse me.
I'm Orlando.

1309
01:18:29,501 --> 01:18:31,002
The line's
over there.

1310
01:18:31,127 --> 01:18:33,004
Where did these ghosts
come from?

1311
01:18:33,129 --> 01:18:34,464
You can hear them, too?

1312
01:18:34,547 --> 01:18:37,467
I hear them in the morning
and the evening.

1313
01:18:37,550 --> 01:18:39,177
They're coming
into the shower.

1314
01:18:39,302 --> 01:18:42,305
Did you tell every spook
you met about me?

1315
01:18:42,389 --> 01:18:45,100
I got spooks from Jersey
coming in here.

1316
01:18:45,225 --> 01:18:47,769
There's stuff going on
you wouldn't believe.

1317
01:18:47,894 --> 01:18:49,813
It's amazing.
You're really doing it.

1318
01:18:50,105 --> 01:18:50,855
I know.

1319
01:18:51,106 --> 01:18:52,774
Can you
hurry this up?

1320
01:18:52,857 --> 01:18:55,110
Oh, chill out.
Chill out.

1321
01:18:55,193 --> 01:18:56,528
I need your help.

1322
01:18:56,611 --> 01:18:58,530
There's something
we need to do.

1323
01:18:58,655 --> 01:19:00,990
I'm not doing anything
else with you, Sam.

1324
01:19:01,116 --> 01:19:02,992
You're holding on
to a life

1325
01:19:03,118 --> 01:19:04,494
that doesn't
want you anymore.

1326
01:19:04,577 --> 01:19:06,746
It doesn't want you.
Give up the ghost.

1327
01:19:06,830 --> 01:19:08,790
Are you speaking
to me?

1328
01:19:08,832 --> 01:19:10,792
Does it look like it?

1329
01:19:10,834 --> 01:19:13,461
You're supposed to be
concentrating, aren't you?

1330
01:19:13,628 --> 01:19:15,130
You going to try it?

1331
01:19:15,171 --> 01:19:16,381
Thank you very much.

1332
01:19:16,506 --> 01:19:18,842
Sam, are you going
to get out of here?

1333
01:19:19,092 --> 01:19:19,843
Uh-uh.

1334
01:19:20,093 --> 01:19:21,428
Fine, then stay there.

1335
01:19:21,511 --> 01:19:22,429
Excuse me.

1336
01:19:22,512 --> 01:19:23,430
Excuse me.

1337
01:19:23,513 --> 01:19:24,806
You ready now?

1338
01:19:24,889 --> 01:19:26,349
Let's do it.

1339
01:19:26,474 --> 01:19:28,810
I got to talk
to you now.

1340
01:19:28,893 --> 01:19:30,353
I've got a plan.

1341
01:19:30,478 --> 01:19:34,107
All we got to do
is we can...

1342
01:19:34,190 --> 01:19:35,316
Oda Mae?

1343
01:19:42,282 --> 01:19:43,533
Oda Mae.

1344
01:19:46,244 --> 01:19:47,203
Ortisha?

1345
01:19:48,621 --> 01:19:50,582
Orlando. Is that you?

1346
01:19:50,665 --> 01:19:53,626
Ortisha, where you at?
I can't hardly see.

1347
01:19:53,710 --> 01:19:54,586
Here.
Sh-She's here.

1348
01:19:54,711 --> 01:19:58,131
In front of you.
I'm right here.

1349
01:20:01,676 --> 01:20:04,929
Damn, baby, what did
you do to your hair?

1350
01:20:07,182 --> 01:20:08,600
Orlando, you like it?

1351
01:20:08,725 --> 01:20:11,227
It's autumn sunrise.

1352
01:20:13,730 --> 01:20:17,233
Get out of me,
you son of a bitch.

1353
01:20:20,362 --> 01:20:22,947
Don't you ever do that
to me again.

1354
01:20:23,198 --> 01:20:24,324
Orlando?

1355
01:20:24,449 --> 01:20:25,784
Ugh!

1356
01:20:25,909 --> 01:20:28,370
I can barely move.

1357
01:20:28,495 --> 01:20:30,288
You should know
better than that.

1358
01:20:30,413 --> 01:20:32,415
Jumping into bodies
wipes you out.

1359
01:20:32,582 --> 01:20:33,458
Everybody out.

1360
01:20:33,583 --> 01:20:34,876
What happened
to Orlando?

1361
01:20:34,959 --> 01:20:37,504
Where's
the insurance policy?

1362
01:20:37,587 --> 01:20:38,922
Are you deaf?

1363
01:20:39,047 --> 01:20:41,424
I said everybody out!

1364
01:20:41,508 --> 01:20:42,676
Everybody out!

1365
